LD(1)                       User Commands                    LD(1)

NAME
    ld - link objects with the linker of tcc

SYNOPSIS
    ld [-o file] [-L dir] [-l name] [-shared] [-static] [-r]
       [-soname name] [-rpath dir] [-Map file] file...

DESCRIPTION
    ld links the named objects, archives and libraries by running
    /bin/tcc -nostdlib. Nothing is added to what is named: a program
    needs /lib/crt1.o, /lib/crti.o and /lib/crtn.o, its libraries and
    /usr/lib/tcc/libtcc1.a on the command line.

OPTIONS
    -o file        write the output to file
    -L dir         add a library directory
    -l name        link libname.so or libname.a
    -shared        produce a shared object
    -static        link statically
    -r             produce a relocatable object
    -soname name   set the soname of a shared object
    -rpath dir     record a run path
    -Map file      write a link map
    -Bsymbolic     bind references inside a shared object to itself
    -e _start, -dynamic-linker /lib/ld.so, -Ttext-segment=0x400000,
    -z ..., --hash-style=..., --as-needed, --start-group, --end-group
                   accepted; they name what tcc does in any case

SEE ALSO
    tcc(1), as(1), ar(1)
